<div class="nav-bar"><a class="nav-link" href="pt_01_UP_向上、完结体、视线显露与靠近.html" title="01_UP_向上、完结体、视线显露与靠近">01 UP <span class="nav-cnt">(645)</span></a><a class="nav-link" href="pt_02_OUT_观察者三视角(消失_显露_丧失)与延展.html" title="02_OUT_观察者三视角(消失/显露/丧失)与延展">02 OUT <span class="nav-cnt">(576)</span></a><a class="nav-link" href="pt_03_OFF_脱离支撑表面、取消切断、起飞引爆与完结.html" title="03_OFF_脱离支撑表面、取消切断、起飞引爆与完结">03 OFF <span class="nav-cnt">(305)</span></a><a class="nav-link" href="pt_04_DOWN_向下、数值减弱、压制瓦解与落笔记录.html" title="04_DOWN_向下、数值减弱、压制瓦解与落笔记录">04 DOWN <span class="nav-cnt">(243)</span></a><a class="nav-link" href="pt_05_IN_功能性包容、状态容器、吸收与向内坍塌.html" title="05_IN_功能性包容、状态容器、吸收与向内坍塌">05 IN <span class="nav-cnt">(246)</span></a><a class="nav-link active" href="pt_06_ON_前行延续(ON²)vs表面支撑_基础_负担(ON¹).html" title="06_ON_前行延续(ON²) vs 表面支撑/基础/负担(ON¹)">06 ON <span class="nav-cnt">(178)</span></a><a class="nav-link" href="pt_07_OVER_弧线跨越、全面审视、翻转倒下与移交克服.html" title="07_OVER_弧线跨越、全面审视、翻转倒下与移交克服">07 OVER <span class="nav-cnt">(133)</span></a><a class="nav-link" href="pt_08_AWAY_远离分离、彻底处置、渐进消逝与持续劳作.html" title="08_AWAY_远离分离、彻底处置、渐进消逝与持续劳作">08 AWAY <span class="nav-cnt">(114)</span></a><a class="nav-link" href="pt_09_BACK_回到起点、对等回击、向后退缩与抑制隐瞒.html" title="09_BACK_回到起点、对等回击、向后退缩与抑制隐瞒">09 BACK <span class="nav-cnt">(101)</span></a><a class="nav-link" href="pt_10_THROUGH_穿过三维通道、熬过难关与彻底审阅.html" title="10_THROUGH_穿过三维通道、熬过难关与彻底审阅">10 THROUGH <span class="nav-cnt">(47)</span></a><a class="nav-link" href="pt_11_AROUND_环绕旋转、漫无目的闲逛、规避与苏醒.html" title="11_AROUND_环绕旋转、漫无目的闲逛、规避与苏醒">11 AROUND <span class="nav-cnt">(72)</span></a><a class="nav-link" href="pt_12_INTO_动态穿越边界、猛烈碰撞、深入调查与形态转化.html" title="12_INTO_动态穿越边界、猛烈碰撞、深入调查与形态转化">12 INTO <span class="nav-cnt">(41)</span></a><a class="nav-link" href="pt_13_其他常见小品词.html" title="13_其他常见小品词">13 其他小品词 <span class="nav-cnt">(365)</span></a></div>
<div class='page-hero'><div><h1 class='hero-title'>06 · ON — 前行延续(ON²) vs 表面支撑/基础/负担(ON¹)<span class='hero-badge'>📖 EPE Ch.3</span></h1><p class='hero-sub'>ON: Forward Continuation (ON²) vs Support, Basis & Burden (ON¹</p></div><div style='font-size:0.88em;color:#475569;font-weight:600;'>共 <b>178</b> 个独立义项 • <b>534</b> 句中英对照例句</div></div>
<details class='epe-book-drawer' open><summary class='epe-drawer-bar'><span>📚 《English Prepositions Explained》(Seth Lindstromberg) 原著核心精讲 — Chapter 3 (On¹, off, on²) & Chapter 4 (§2.1, §3.3)</span><span style='font-size:0.84em;color:#6366f1;font-weight:600;'>点击收起 / 展开原书理论图式 ▾</span></summary><div class='epe-drawer-grid'><div class='epe-box-card'><div class='epe-box-title'>🧭 原著空间与功能核心图式 (Core Schema)</div><div><b>EPE 核心创见：必须严格区分两个截然不同的词 —— ON¹（接触与支撑，反义词 OFF）与 ON²（面向前方继续推进，反义词 BACK）</b>！ON¹ 的本质是主体接触支撑面（若撤去支撑面主体会坠落）；ON² 则专作不及物小品词，表示沿着既定方向克服停顿继续前进。</div><div class='epe-box-title' style='margin-top:12px;'>📝 原书典型语料例句 (Authentic Examples from EPE)</div><div class='epe-quote-chip'>📌 <i>As they carried on toward the setting sun...</i> (ON² 贡献“暂停后凭决心继续向目标推进”，TOWARD 贡献“当前朝向”) [Ch.3 (26)]</div><div class='epe-quote-chip'>📌 <i>Getting the job depends on your performance at the interview.</i> (为什么不说 *depend from？因为英语将面试表现视为支撑结果的基座 Basis) [Ch.1 §7 & Ch.3 (43)]</div></div><div class='epe-box-card'><div class='epe-box-title'>⚖️ 原书近义小品词深度辨析与隐喻机制 (Key Contrasts & Metaphors)</div><ul class='epe-contrast-list'><li><b>ON² vs ALONG / OFF / AWAY (Ch.3 §8.1 经典四车对比)</b>：<i>The car sped on</i>（ON²：<b>暗示刚才曾受阻减速或停顿，现克服干扰继续沿原路线前进</b>） vs <i>sped along</i>（顺畅巡航，无受阻暗示） vs <i>sped off</i>（离开原本停靠的地面点） vs <i>sped away</i>（距离观察者越来越远）。</li><li><b>ON¹ 负担隐喻 (The Burden Metaphor — Ch.3 §9.1.2 Fig.3.8)</b>：把倒霉事视为压在受害者背上的重石（<i>My car died on me; She gave up on me; draw a gun on sb; blow the whistle on sb; go back on one's word</i>）。</li><li><b>ON¹ 基础隐喻 (The Basis Metaphor — Ch.3 §9.1.6)</b>：把某事物视为雕像底座（plinth）或房屋地基（foundation），抽走就会垮塌（<i>depend/rely/hinge/count/build/capitalize on; succeed on the back of innovation</i>）。</li><li><b>ON¹ 猛扑与缓冲接触 (Ch.3 §9.1.3–9.1.4 Fig.3.9)</b>：如猫从高处扑向老鼠（<i>pounce/jump on sb; hit on an idea/a girl</i>）；<i>tap on something</i> 比直接 <i>tap something</i> 多了一层缓冲垫，动作更表层。</li></ul></div></div></details>

